# This file lives at the repo root — prettier's DEFAULT --ignore-path location — on
# purpose. Under config/ it only applied when a caller passed
# `--ignore-path config/.prettierignore`, so a bare `npx prettier --write .` saw no
# ignore list at all and happily rewrote generated files (theme.css below).

# dependencies and builds
node_modules
.turbo
.cache
dist
build
coverage
.vscode
out

# generated artifacts
*.tsbuildinfo
# theme.css is generated by `pnpm build:theme` (sync-css-theme.ts) using prettier's
# default CSS formatting and byte-verified by buildThemeCss.test.ts — keep it out of
# the config-prettier check, whose CSS rules would otherwise conflict with the generator.
# Reformatting it is unrecoverable by tooling: the generator re-runs only when its
# source changes, so `pnpm build:theme` reports "up to date" while the output is wrong.
**/main/kernel/ui/src/styles/theme.css
**/main/kernel/db/src/**/*.d.ts
**/main/kernel/db/src/**/*.d.ts.map
**/main/kernel/db/src/**/*.js
**/main/kernel/db/src/**/*.js.map
# The oracle snapshots are written by `pnpm bslt snapshot <id>` as plain two-space JSON and
# compared byte for byte by their gates. Prettier would collapse their short arrays.
**/main/tools/snapshots/*.json
# The database catalog, written by `pnpm bslt db catalog` in the same form.
**/main/kernel/db/catalog.snapshot.json
# The OpenAPI document, written by `pnpm bslt sync openapi` in the same form.
**/docs/reference/openapi.json
playwright-report
test-results
**/tests/e2e/reports/**
.playwright-mcp/

